  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/recovery/assets/ab2f3a9137c05ca19507e44d2bb2ef4b369c762189019265d8fe3bad34822fe7.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg\u2061(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{6}{11})=0.499\\,346\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg\u2061(z)=\\pi +0.499\\,346\u2026\u22483.64,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
